-- title:
--   Atkin–Lehner involution preserves integrality over R[j]
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ and $p$ be natural numbers with $N \neq 0$ and $p$ prime, and assume $p \nmid N$. Write $F = \mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFull}(Np)$ for the intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q} \subseteq \mathbb{Q}((q))$ (Laurent series over $\mathbb{Q}$) generated by the set of all $q$-expansions $\mathrm{qExpand}\,\mathbb{Q}\,d\,\mathrm{jq}$, i.e. $j(q^{d})$, as $d$ runs over the nonzero divisors of $Np$, where $\mathrm{jq}$ is the Laurent series $q^{-1}$ times the rationalised numerator power series of the $j$-invariant. Let $R$ be a commutative ring equipped with algebra structures on $\mathbb{Q}$ and on $F$ such that $R \to \mathbb{Q} \to F$ is a scalar tower, and let $J \in F$ denote $\mathrm{jq}$ itself, a member of $F$. Then for every $x \in F$ that is integral over the $R$-subalgebra $\mathrm{Algebra.adjoin}\,R\,\{J\} \subseteq F$, the image $\mathrm{atkinLehnerInvolutionFull}\,N\,p\,(x)$ is again integral over that same subalgebra. Here $\mathrm{atkinLehnerInvolutionFull}\,N\,p$ is the $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra automorphism of $F$ chosen, if one exists, to interchange $j(q^{d})$ with $j(q^{dp})$ for every nonzero $d \mid N$, and the identity otherwise.
--
--   This is the ring-theoretic content of the assertion that the partial Atkin–Lehner involution $w_p$ of the function field of $X_0(Np)$ preserves the integral closure of $R[j]$, i.e. extends to the normalisation of the $j$-line over $R$ away from the cusps, uniformly in the base ring $R$. It is used in the construction of integral models and charts for $X_0(Np)$, in particular by the results on Deligne–Rapoport and Igusa charts that compare the involution with local coordinate algebras and valuation subrings.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_isIntegral_adjoin_jq_atkinLehnerInvolutionFull.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_AtkinLehnerPartial

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

open ModularCurve

theorem ModularCurve.isIntegral_adjoin_jq_atkinLehnerInvolutionFull
    (N p : ℕ) [NeZero N] [Fact p.Prime] (hpN : ¬ p ∣ N)
    (R : Type*) [CommRing R] [Algebra R ℚ] [Algebra R (modularFunctionFieldFull (N * p))]
    [IsScalarTower R ℚ (modularFunctionFieldFull (N * p))]
    (x : modularFunctionFieldFull (N * p))
    (hx : IsIntegral
      (Algebra.adjoin R ({⟨jq, modularFunctionField_le_full (N * p) (jq_mem (N * p))⟩} :
        Set (modularFunctionFieldFull (N * p)))) x) :
    IsIntegral
      (Algebra.adjoin R ({⟨jq, modularFunctionField_le_full (N * p) (jq_mem (N * p))⟩} :
        Set (modularFunctionFieldFull (N * p))))
      (atkinLehnerInvolutionFull N p x) := by sorry
